# `.taurignore` — Tauri CLI ignore patterns.
#
# The Tauri CLI uses the `ignore` crate (via `ignore::WalkBuilder`) to
# walk the project tree for two things: the `tauri dev` file watcher
# (notify) and the icon / source-file discovery at build time. Both
# open a file descriptor per directory entry while iterating, and
# the Tauri CLI does **not** apply a `max_open(1)` or equivalent
# back-pressure. On a project whose `target/` and `node_modules/`
# together contain tens of thousands of files, that walker can
# exhaust the per-process file-descriptor limit and panic with
# `Error { kind: Io(Os { code: 24, kind: Uncategorized, message: "Too
# many open files" }) }` at `crates/tauri-cli/src/interface/rust.rs`
# line 146 (the `Result::unwrap()` on the walker iterator).
#
# The Tauri CLI is a precompiled native Node addon bundled in
# `node_modules/@tauri-apps/cli-linux-x64-gnu/`, so we cannot patch
# the walker ourselves. The supported fix is to add this file
# (Tauri CLI looks for `.taurignore` in every directory it walks
# and applies the patterns in addition to the built-in defaults).
#
# Syntax: gitignore-compatible (the Tauri CLI uses the `ignore`
# crate, which supports the same patterns as `.gitignore`).

# Build artefacts — by far the largest source of FD pressure.
# `target/` holds every compiled `.rmeta`, `.rlib`, and intermediate
# Cargo output for every workspace member; a release build easily
# pushes past 20k files. Tauri never needs to read anything from
# `target/` after `cargo build` finishes.
target/
**/target/

# Node modules — never needed at build time; the frontend is already
# bundled into `dist/` by Vite before Tauri sees it.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# Vite / frontend build output. Tauri reads `dist/` via the
# `frontendDist` config option directly, not by walking.
dist/

# Crash dumps (Tauri/webview segfaults on this OS occasionally).
coredump/

# README / docs screenshots.
images/

# Editor / OS metadata.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local agent scratch (Plannotator sessions etc.).
.pi/

# Notes from past sessions.
notes/
*.log
